[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:A Private Conversation]
[00:00.68]Why did the writer complain to the people behind him? | 作者为什么要向他身后的人抱怨？
[00:14.97]Last week I went to the theatre. | 上周我去了剧院。
[00:19.10]I had a very good seat. | 我有一个很好的座位。
[00:21.82]The play was very interesting. | 戏很有趣。
[00:24.74]I did not enjoy it. | 我却没有享受到乐趣。
[00:27.12]A young man and a young woman were sitting behind me. | 一对年轻的男女坐在我身后。
[00:31.72]They were talking loudly. | 他们大声地说着话。
[00:34.16]I got very angry. | 我非常生气。
[00:37.12]I could not hear the actors. | 我听不见演员的讲话。
[00:40.30]I turned round. | 我转过身。
[00:42.40]I looked at the man and the woman angrily. | 我怒气冲冲地看着那一男一女。
[00:46.80]They did not pay any attention. | 他们却不理不睬。
[00:50.34]In the end, I could not bear it. | 最后，我忍不住了。
[00:54.62]I turned round again. | 我又转过身去。
[00:57.34]'I can't hear a word!' I said angrily. | “我一个字也听不见了！”我生气地说。
[01:02.75]'It's none of your business,' | “不关你的事，”
[01:06.02]the young man said rudely. | 那个年轻人粗鲁地说。
[01:08.54]'This is a private conversation!' | “这是私人谈话！”